Progress update — Phase 16 local implementation, 2026-10-12 UTC:
- Added producer/consumer hook contexts, Java ACL signing, Java trace record model/encoder, trace fixtures and bounded dispatcher; producer Pub/EndTransaction/Recall and consumer SubBefore/SubAfter paths now have local coverage. Recall support was absent from the initial implementation and has now been added: Java-compatible URL-safe handle build/decode, `Producer::recall_message`, request/response headers, one-attempt `RECALL_MESSAGE` RPC, namespaced topic, broker-name route with topic fallback, and the recall RPC trace hook. The recall RPC hook is registered only when producer tracing is enabled and the Java boolean property `com.rocketmq.recall.default.trace.enable` is true; it is removed on producer shutdown.
- Formatting check first found two rustfmt differences in producer trace code; `cargo fmt --all` fixed them and the subsequent `cargo fmt --all -- --check` passed. The first compile of recall code found Base64 was only a dev dependency; moved it to Producer's normal dependencies. `cargo check -p rocketmq-classic-producer -p rocketmq-classic-core -p rocketmq-classic --locked` then passed.
- Recall tests passed: Producer unit filter (8 tests, including handle decoding, trace fields/property parsing, hook lifecycle, and producer validation), Core RPC filter (2 scripted peer tests), and Protocol header filter (1 test). Full `cargo test -p rocketmq-classic-producer --locked` passed (74 unit + 17 integration tests); full `cargo test -p rocketmq-classic-consumer --locked` passed (140 unit + 35 integration tests).
- `mvn -f compat/java-reference/pom.xml verify` passed after adding ACL/trace fixture generators; it validated 32 scenarios and completed Java 5.5.1 invoked fixture checks, including trace, ACL and generated typed headers/bodies.
- Remaining Phase 16 local work is still open: reconcile namespace behavior across every path against source/tests; add the required TLS scripted failure matrix (unreadable/malformed material, wrong name, expired certificate, unsupported handshake and missing client certificate); verify channel-event bounded observer/shutdown behavior; complete trace overflow/size/flush evidence; update security/usage docs and compatibility matrix; then run the Phase 16 workspace/all-features gate and commit. Phase 17 and Phase 18 have not started. Phase 19 Broker/Docker validation remains a later handoff.
- Follow-up local security/event work: `RemotingClient::with_config` now constructs a TLS connector once before retaining worker receivers, so malformed client identity material fails before `start()`. Added scripted security tests for unreadable credential paths, malformed client identity, expired server certificate, TLS-to-plaintext handshake, and required-but-missing client certificate. `cargo test -p rocketmq-classic-remoting --test security --locked` passed all 5. Existing CA/name verification, untrusted CA, and Java trust-all tests passed (2 + 1). Added `p16_slow_channel_observer_does_not_block_transport_and_is_cancelled_on_shutdown`; it passed. The explicit slow-observer case confirms remoting response completion is independent of the event worker; cancellation on shutdown follows the previously accepted Phase 3 disposition and is not claimed as Java shutdown-drain parity.

