- Extended `pull_routes_per_queue_returns_decoded_messages_and_only_explicitly_persists_offsets` to assert the offset store update/read/persist keys use `tenant%orders`, while the Broker pull already asserts the namespaced group and topic. The targeted locked test passed.
- Added `trace_flush_waits_for_scripted_broker_delivery`; a scripted NameServer/Broker accepts and acknowledges the encoded trace message before dispatcher `flush()` returns. `cargo test -p rocketmq-classic-producer --test scripted_send trace_flush_waits_for_scripted_broker_delivery --locked` passed.
- Added `docs/security.md` with namespace, ACL, TLS, hooks, tracing, and channel-event usage notes; updated the Phase 16 compatibility row with the new test evidence.
- Still open: complete the Java 5.5.1 source/API/settings-to-test audit for all Phase 16 namespace routes, hooks, ACL, TLS, trace and event behavior; reconcile any remaining gaps; run the final Phase 16 gates after the full audit; commit Phase 16 before creating the Phase 17 branch. Phase 17/18 and the Phase 6 final reconciliation remain outstanding. Phase 19 live Broker/Docker evidence remains a later handoff.

